  "id": "congenital-cataract",
  "term": "congenital cataract",
  "definition": "Congenital cataract is a clouding of the eye’s lens that is present at birth, usually linked to genetic causes or environmental influences such as rubella infection during early pregnancy. It is a major treatable cause of childhood blindness and visual impairment and may be found on routine examination or when signs such as a white pupil or eye misalignment are noticed.",
